---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = "How to Calculate the Time Between Two Times - Toolkit Lab";
const description = "How to work out hours and minutes between two times, handle shifts that cross midnight, and convert the result to decimal hours for timesheets.";
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/guides/how-to-calculate-time-between-two-times">
  <aside class="ad-rail" aria-label="Advertisement"><div class="ad-slot ad-slot-rail"></div></aside>
  <div class="wrap article">
    <p class="note"><a href="/guides">Guides</a> / Time</p>
    <h1>How to Calculate the Time Between Two Times</h1>
    <p class="lead">Subtracting one clock time from another is simple until a shift crosses midnight or you need decimal hours for a timesheet. A few rules cover both cases.</p>
    <div class="ad-slot" aria-label="Advertisement"></div>
<h2>Subtract the start from the end</h2>
<p>Convert both times to minutes after midnight, then subtract. 09:30 is 570 minutes and 17:15 is 1,035 minutes, so the difference is 465 minutes, which is 7 hours and 45 minutes.</p>
<h2>Shifts that cross midnight</h2>
<p>If the end time is earlier than the start, add 24 hours to the end. A shift from 22:00 to 06:00 is 8 hours. Add 24 hours to 06:00, which gives 1,800 minutes, and subtract 22:00, which is 1,320 minutes. The difference is 480 minutes, or 8 hours.</p>
<h2>Decimal hours for timesheets</h2>
<p>Divide the minutes by 60. 7 hours and 45 minutes is 7.75 hours. A 15-minute break is 0.25 hours, so it is easy to subtract. Many payroll systems use decimal hours, so check which format your employer uses.</p>
<h2>Try it yourself</h2>
<p>The <a href="/tools/time-duration-calculator">Time Duration Calculator</a> handles overnight shifts and shows hours and minutes plus decimal hours.</p>
      <section class="worked">
        <h2>Worked example</h2>
        <p>From 09:30 to 17:15: 09:30 is 570 minutes after midnight and 17:15 is 1,035 minutes, a difference of 465 minutes, or 7 hours 45 minutes. In decimal hours that is 7.75.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="faq-list">
        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <details><summary>How do I take off a break?</summary><p>Subtract the break from the total. For a 30-minute break, 7.75 hours minus 0.5 hours is 7.25 hours.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How are overnight shifts calculated?</summary><p>Add 24 hours to the end time if it is earlier than the start. A shift from 22:00 to 06:00 is 8 hours.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Should I use 12-hour or 24-hour times?</summary><p>Either works, but 24-hour times avoid confusion between morning and evening, especially for overnight shifts.</p></details>
      </section>
